(ned -- SHOULDER FIND, the last step of calibration. Operator 2026-08-03.)
(Everything up to here is ned's own calibration. This step hands the result)
(to Probe Basic and then uses PB's OWN stock routine for the shoulder, which)
(is the only PB-native part of the exercise.)

(WHAT GETS SENT TO PB)
(  #5181/#5182/#5183 -- the tool-setter position PB drives to. These ARE)
(     LinuxCNC's G30 position, which is why G30.1 sets them: park on the)
(     point and record it. No work-to-machine conversion to get wrong.)
(  #3007 -- max Z plunge, 215 mm. The longest tool sits 180 mm from the)
(     shoulder; 185 did not reach, so the allowance went up by 30.)
(  #3010 -- the SHOULDER itself, written by PB's probe_spindle_nose.)

(THE TWO HEIGHTS, which are different and easy to confuse)
(  tool probing starts at puck top + 100 mm: with a probe rod in and touching)
(     the setter, there is then 100 mm of clearance above it. That is the Z)
(     recorded into G30.)
(  the shoulder is probed at X -20 from the puck centre, because the spindle)
(     nose is a ring -- probing on the centreline would meet the taper bore,)
(     not the face.)

(REQUIRES AN EMPTY SPINDLE. The caller checks and refuses; this is the)
(shoulder, so anything in the taper is what would get measured instead.)

o<cal_shoulder> sub
  #<cx>   = #1
  #<cy>   = #2
  #<top>  = #3
  #<zmin> = #4        (Z soft limit, passed from the INI by the caller)

  (THE PACKET SENT TO PB, held as saved parameters so it is visible and)
  (stored where it corresponds to what actually goes across -- operator)
  (2026-08-03. Seeded on first use so an empty var file still works.)
  (  #3076 = Z clearance above the rod-measured top -> the G30 height)
  (  #3077 = the plunge actually used, mirrored for display)
  (  #3078 = X offset from centre for the nose probe)
  o1 if [#3076 EQ 0]
    #3076 = 100.0
  o1 endif
  o3 if [#3078 EQ 0]
    #3078 = -20.0
  o3 endif
  #<zclear>  = #3076
  #<xoff>    = #3078

  (PLUNGE IS COMPUTED AFTER G30.1, BELOW, AND NOT HERE. It used to be)
  (worked out at this point as [top + zclear] - [zmin + 1], and those two)
  (terms are in DIFFERENT FRAMES: `top` is a WORK Z handed in by the caller,)
  (`zmin` is the MACHINE soft limit out of the INI. Subtracting one from the)
  (other buries the active G54 Z offset in the answer.)
  (2026-08-11, measured: top -272.698 work, offset -157.213, zmin -620.)
  (  computed  [-272.698 + 100] - [-620 + 1] = 446.302)
  (  available [-429.911 + 100] - [-620 + 1] = 289.089)
  (  the 157.213 difference IS the offset.)
  (So PB was told to drive 157 mm further than Z can go and the cycle died on)
  (the soft limit instead of touching the shoulder -- and because the error is)
  (a FUNCTION of the offset, it appeared the moment the puck was re-zeroed.)
  (The header of this file already states the principle: #5181/2/3 are the)
  (G30 position, machine, "no work-to-machine conversion to get wrong". G30.1)
  (below records exactly the start height, so #5183 IS that height in machine)
  (terms. Subtract the machine limit from it and both sides finally agree.)
  #<f_tr>    = 2000.0

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, SHOULDER: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, SHOULDER: no puck centre - run the calibration first)
  o6 endif

  M50 P0

  (--- 1. record the tool-setter position into G30 -----------------------)
  (XY first, then Z, exactly as everywhere else: the head rests over the)
  (puck and Z must not move until it is laterally clear.)
  G90
  G1 X#<cx> Y#<cy> F[#<f_tr>]
  G1 Z[#<top> + #<zclear>] F[#<f_tr>]
  G30.1
  (PRINT, SHOULDER: tool-setter position recorded to G30 - X #5181 Y #5182 Z #5183 machine. That is the puck centre at top plus #<zclear> mm.)

  (--- 2. the plunge allowance PB will use ------------------------------)
  (MACHINE MINUS MACHINE. #5183 was just written by G30.1 above and is the)
  (start height in machine coordinates; zmin is the machine soft limit. Stop)
  (1 mm short of it, so the plunge can never be the thing that trips the)
  (limit. Operator 2026-08-11: just automatically go to the soft limit of Z)
  (plus 1mm so that stupid soft limit does not arise.)
  #<plunge> = [#5183 - [#<zmin> + 1.0]]
  #3077 = #<plunge>
  o4 if [#<plunge> LE 0]
    (abort, SHOULDER: no room to plunge - the start height is already at the Z soft limit.)
  o4 endif
  #3007 = #<plunge>
  (PRINT, SHOULDER: max plunge #3007 mm sent to PB - from G30 Z #5183 machine down to 1 mm above the #<zmin> soft limit.)

  (--- 3. over the shoulder probing point -------------------------------)
  G1 X[#<cx> + #<xoff>] Y#<cy> F[#<f_tr>]
  (PRINT, SHOULDER: at X #<xoff> from centre, probing down up to #<plunge> mm. Spindle must be EMPTY.)

  (--- 4. PB\'s own routine. Untouched: it probes straight down from where)
  (--- it stands and writes #3010, the spindle zero height.)
  M64 P3
  G4 P1.5
  o<probe_spindle_nose> call
  M65 P3

  (PRINT, SHOULDER DONE: spindle zero height #3010 mm. PB now has the setter position, the plunge limit and the shoulder - ready for tool length probing.)
  (DEBUG, SHOULDER DONE: #3010 mm - PB ready)

o<cal_shoulder> endsub

M2 (end program)
